00:32:35.820 --> 00:32:37.800
And it's kind of interesting
'cause are they chosen,

00:32:37.800 --> 00:32:40.590
you know, like a politician
elected in a district has,

00:32:40.590 --> 00:32:43.140
you know, very clear
mandates like schools,

00:32:43.140 --> 00:32:44.190
stuff for that district.

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:46.470
Those are the people that're
gonna elect them versus

00:32:46.470 --> 00:32:48.270
someone who's chosen by lottery.

00:32:48.270 --> 00:32:49.980
They feel like they need
to be representative,

00:32:49.980 --> 00:32:51.930
but sometimes it varies by person.

00:32:51.930 --> 00:32:53.430
So they need to represent
their class, they need

00:32:53.430 --> 00:32:54.780
to represent their geographic area.

00:32:54.780 --> 00:32:57.600
But it's much, it's much more expansive.

00:32:57.600 --> 00:33:01.440
But there still is a
level of responsibility.

00:33:01.440 --> 00:33:02.490
And so that's what Theo's working on.

00:33:02.490 --> 00:33:05.910
So everyone go talk to Theo,
he'll be here at some point.

00:33:05.910 --> 00:33:07.203
So I think that's true.

00:33:08.430 --> 00:33:09.420
And what's interesting is,

00:33:09.420 --> 00:33:11.700
so like in the historical cases, you know,

00:33:11.700 --> 00:33:13.260
we're looking like Brendan

00:33:13.260 --> 00:33:15.450
and I are looking at a wide range.

00:33:15.450 --> 00:33:16.622
And what's interesting is like the idea

00:33:16.622 --> 00:33:18.960
of representation also changes, right?

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:22.110
So like from ancient Greece
to then 19th century Europe,

00:33:22.110 --> 00:33:24.510
like 19th century Europe
politicians, they were like,

00:33:24.510 --> 00:33:26.640
well I know best I'm going to do these,

00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:28.487
but these were elites who
thought that, you know,

00:33:28.487 --> 00:33:30.690
we are kind of in the era of should,

00:33:30.690 --> 00:33:32.940
should citizens even be
involved in this, right?

00:33:32.940 --> 00:33:35.220
So they had an idea of a mandate.

00:33:35.220 --> 00:33:38.190
But the mandate was, you know, I am elite,

00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:39.810
I can decide this for the people.

00:33:39.810 --> 00:33:42.330
But there still was kind of
this idea of representation.

00:33:42.330 --> 00:33:47.310
And we had, so the, one

00:33:47.310 --> 00:33:50.130
of the policymakers that was
instrumental in setting up

00:33:50.130 --> 00:33:52.080
the Belgian committees was
here a couple weeks ago.

00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:55.620
Jonathan Movic super,
super interesting work.

00:33:55.620 --> 00:33:58.740
And he was talking about also
it depends on the politician.

00:33:58.740 --> 00:34:00.630
So some politicians that
have participated in these

00:34:00.630 --> 00:34:04.110
deliberative committees
and the politicians can

00:34:04.110 --> 00:34:05.940
self-select in, which is important.

00:34:05.940 --> 00:34:08.130
So the citizens are chosen randomly,

00:34:08.130 --> 00:34:09.900
but the politicians who work on the issue

00:34:09.900 --> 00:34:11.910
or who want to do that self-select.

00:34:11.910 --> 00:34:13.650
So again, the selection effect.

00:34:13.650 --> 00:34:16.290
So, and theoretically these
politicians would be the one

00:34:16.290 --> 00:34:18.630
who are interested in this, wanna learn.

00:34:18.630 --> 00:34:23.520
Some politicians are, you know,
they believe in the cause.

00:34:23.520 --> 00:34:25.590
They believe in this type
of democratic innovation.

00:34:25.590 --> 00:34:26.430
They believe in the structure,

00:34:26.430 --> 00:34:27.570
they believe they can learn something.

00:34:27.570 --> 00:34:30.570
So they go into it being open to updating

00:34:30.570 --> 00:34:32.070
and open to listening to citizens.

00:34:32.070 --> 00:34:34.080
And they said other
politicians are doing it

00:34:34.080 --> 00:34:36.000
for the photo op basically.

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:38.580
And so that's not a
politician versus citizen,

00:34:38.580 --> 00:34:41.130
that's variation within
individual politicians.

00:34:41.130 --> 00:34:43.290
And what's interesting is that in Belgium,

00:34:43.290 --> 00:34:45.480
it's the green party, or at least the,

00:34:45.480 --> 00:34:46.860
Jonathan was working with the green party.

00:34:46.860 --> 00:34:49.680
So the climate, the
liberal, like, you know,

00:34:49.680 --> 00:34:52.050
those politicians really
believe in the cause

00:34:52.050 --> 00:34:54.930
and are kind of open to
it while other politicians

00:34:54.930 --> 00:34:56.460
doing other topics are less.

00:34:56.460 --> 00:34:58.650
So some of this might not be as level as

00:34:58.650 --> 00:35:01.410
it might be individual
variation, like, you know,

00:35:01.410 --> 00:35:03.900
convince politicians that
this is a good exercise,

00:35:03.900 --> 00:35:07.350
maybe they will be less likely
to dominate the discussion.

00:35:07.350 --> 00:35:09.630
